    "description": "The integration work changes the data model that was originally scoped and demonstrated. Anyone who has already tested against the earlier model will see differences.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n* Links become their own object (Deal_Link__c) rather than a text field on the assignment\n\n* Assignment history captures more than status — link changes and periods too\n\n* The Deal record gains readiness fields (Sync_Ready\\__c, Ready_to_Publishc, Sync_Readiness_Issuesc) and sync fields (CMS_Sync_Status_\\_c and friends)\n\n* Update test scripts covering deal setup, link management and assignment history\n\n* WALK THE CHANGES THROUGH WITH UAT PARTICIPANTS rather than letting them discover them mid-cycle\n\n* Applies whether or not the integration is live at go-live — the data model changes happen either way\n\nEffort: \\~4-8h.\n\nSource: CMS Integration Design v1, §11.5.",
